<%# locals: (matchup:, multiplier:, opponents:) %>
<%# A multi-week pick is a TEAM, not a game — so this card leads with the team
    and its ONE span multiplier (derived from expected points across every week),
    and carries the three opponents underneath as supporting detail.

    The card wears the team's own colors: a team-hue gradient field, the city on
    a small line above the mascot in a bold accent. A team's color_disposition
    decides which brand color is the field vs the mascot — light-disposition
    teams (the gold Saints, the red Bucs) flip the two. See
    TeamColorsHelper#team_card_palette for how the brand fields become CSS.

    `matchup` is the team's WEEK-ONE matchup: it is the anchor the selection is
    keyed on, so toggleSelection / selections[] work exactly as they do on a
    single-week board. `opponents` is [[week, matchup_or_nil], ...] in week
    order; a nil matchup is a bye. %>
<% locked = matchup.locked? %>
<% team = matchup.team %>
<%# Each opponent column is labelled with the DAY that game is played rather
    than its week number — the span is named all over this page already, so the
    column is free to answer "when do I watch this one" instead of repeating it.
    The week is not lost: it moves into the tooltip and the accessible name
    (`detail`). Resolved once, here, so the chip, the tooltip and the aria-label
    can never disagree — and via ContestsHelper#game_day_label, which reads the
    kickoff in US EASTERN. A UTC read prints TOMORROW on every night game. %>
<% opponent_slots = opponents.map do |week, week_matchup|
     opponent_slot_labels(week, week_matchup)
       .merge(matchup: week_matchup, opponent: week_matchup&.opponent_team)
   end %>
<% pal = team_card_palette(team) %>
<% glow_alt = team.color_alt.presence || team.color_light %>
<div class="holo-wrap relative" style="--glow-c: <%= glow_alt %>;">
  <%# Animated glowing border: a conic-gradient wedge in the team's alt/light
      color rotates behind the card; the opaque card covers the center, leaving a
      bright rotating ring, with a blurred twin for bloom. On hover + selected. %>
  <span class="holo-border-glow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span class="holo-border" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <button x-data="{ pressing: false, releasing: false, hoverLocked: false }"
        @click="toggleSelection('<%= matchup.id %>'); if (selections['<%= matchup.id %>']) { hoverLocked = false; pressing = true; setTimeout(() => pressing = false, 360) } else { releasing = true; hoverLocked = true; setTimeout(() => releasing = false, 450) }"
        @mouseleave="hoverLocked = false"
        class="holo-card relative w-full p-3 md:p-4 rounded-2xl text-center border-2 shadow overflow-hidden <%= locked ? 'opacity-50' : '' %>"
        style="background: <%= pal[:gradient] %>; border-color: <%= pal[:border] %>; color: <%= pal[:fg] %>; --glow-soft: <%= rgba(pal[:glow], 0.3) %>;"
        :class="{
          'is-selected': selections['<%= matchup.id %>'],
          'is-pressing': pressing,
          'is-releasing': releasing,
          'hover-locked': hoverLocked,
          'shine-off': selectionCount > 0,
          'matchup-pulse': pulseId === '<%= matchup.id %>' && selectionCount === 0
        }"
        role="checkbox" :aria-checked="!!selections['<%= matchup.id %>']"
        aria-label="<%= team.name %> — <%= opponent_slots.map { |slot| "#{slot[:detail]}: #{slot[:opponent]&.name || 'bye'}" }.join(', ') %>"
        <% if locked %>disabled<% end %>>
  <% if locked %>
    <span class="absolute top-2 left-2 text-[10px]" style="color: <%= pal[:fg_faint] %>">&#128274;</span>
  <% end %>

  <%# City small + lighter, mascot large + bold in the team accent. Two lines
      also cure the old single-line truncation ("San Francisco 49...",
      "Los Angeles Char..."). %>
  <% if team.location.present? %>
    <p class="text-xs md:text-sm font-medium leading-tight truncate"
       style="color: <%= pal[:location] %>" title="<%= team.name %>"><%= team.location %></p>
  <% end %>
  <p class="font-extrabold text-2xl md:text-3xl leading-tight truncate team-name"
     style="color: <%= pal[:accent] %>; text-shadow: <%= pal[:mascot_shadow] %>" title="<%= team.name %>"><%= team.mascot %></p>

  <%# One line: the stylish multiplier (1.6x) then the "Points" label.
      THE MULTIPLIER SIGN IS A LOWERCASE x, AND IT IS NOT IN THE MONO SPAN.
      Both halves of that were the fix for a sign that read as floating.
      U+00D7 (×) is hung on the font's MATH AXIS, roughly half the cap height,
      so it rides high beside a digit instead of sitting with it — and inside
      the monospace face it is additionally drawn small in a full character
      cell, which detaches it further. Worst after a lone "1". A lowercase x
      in the card's own sans face sits on the baseline at x-height, one size
      below the digits, and reads as part of the number.

      The digits stay monospace — that is the look on the rest of the board.
      The two spans are butted with NO whitespace between the tags; the
      newline before "Points" is what supplies that one word space.

      "Points" IS UNCONDITIONAL. The number multiplies points, it does not
      count them, so "1x Point" was never right: 1x is one TIMES points. %>
  <% if multiplier %>
    <p class="mt-1.5">
      <span class="font-mono font-bold text-lg md:text-xl" style="color: <%= pal[:fg] %>"><%= format_turf_score(multiplier) %></span><span class="font-bold text-base md:text-lg" style="color: <%= pal[:fg] %>">x</span>
      <span class="text-sm" style="color: <%= pal[:fg_faint] %>">Points</span>
    </p>
  <% end %>

  <%# "vs" rides the divider so the three chips read as who this team faces.
      It wears the card's own foreground at the multiplier's weight, so the
      multiplier and this line are the two bold marks down the card's spine.
      The word it replaced sat in faint grey and was five syllables long — it
      competed with the dates below it for the same quiet ink and won, while
      saying less.

      grid-template-columns is inline rather than a Tailwind grid-cols-N class
      so a span of any length lays out evenly (a 2- or 4-week contest would
      otherwise need a class that isn't compiled). %>
  <div class="mt-3 flex items-center gap-2" aria-hidden="true">
    <span class="h-px flex-1" style="background-color: <%= pal[:divider] %>"></span>
    <span class="text-xs font-bold" style="color: <%= pal[:fg] %>">vs</span>
    <span class="h-px flex-1" style="background-color: <%= pal[:divider] %>"></span>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-2 grid" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(<%= [opponent_slots.size, 1].max %>, minmax(0, 1fr))">
    <% opponent_slots.each_with_index do |slot, index| %>
      <% opponent = slot[:opponent] %>
      <div class="tm-opponent-cell px-px lg:px-1 text-center"
           style="<%= "border-left: 1px solid #{pal[:divider]};" if index.positive? %>"
           title="<%= slot[:detail] %> &mdash; <%= opponent ? "vs #{opponent.name}" : 'bye week' %>">
        <%# The date ("Dec 25"), or the week when that game has no kickoff yet.
            Both fit the width "WEEK 16" already held, so the mobile column
            budget the sizes below were tuned against is unchanged. %>
        <p class="tm-opponent-week text-[9px] lg:text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wide leading-tight" style="color: <%= pal[:grey] %>"><%= slot[:shown] %></p>
        <%# emoji + abbreviation share one centered baseline (items-center,
            leading-none) so the taller emoji stops leaving vertical space above
            the text; the abbreviation wears the opponent's own color.

            Sizes are mobile-first and deliberately small. A column here is
            one third of a card, and the card is one of TWO across a phone
            (grid-cols-2) — ~48px at a 390px viewport. An unconditional text-sm
            needed ~46px for emoji + gap + abbreviation and blew that, so
            `truncate` ate the short name down to a single letter ("I…"),
            hiding the opponent this row exists to name.

            The step is at `lg`, NOT `md`, because the size that matters is the
            CARD's, not the viewport's: the grid goes grid-cols-2 → md:grid-cols-4,
            so a card is ~172px at 768px — the SAME width it has on a phone —
            and only reaches ~236px at 1024px. Sizing on `md` therefore made the
            768-1023px band the worst case of all (every abbreviation clipped);
            `lg` moves the bump to where the card actually grows.

            10px emoji + 10px abbreviation clear the widest short name ("WAS")
            with room at 375px and up; below that `truncate` still degrades it,
            as it did before. %>
        <%# The halo rides the ROW, behind emoji and abbreviation together, and
            the row stays a full-width block so the gradient can fade out
            inside the column. See TeamColorsHelper#opponent_label_halo. %>
        <p class="tm-opponent-row mt-1 py-1 flex items-center justify-center gap-0.5 lg:gap-1 leading-none"
           style="background: <%= opponent_label_halo(opponent, team) %>">
          <% if opponent %>
            <span class="text-[10px] lg:text-sm"><%= opponent.emoji %></span>
            <span class="text-[10px] lg:text-sm font-semibold truncate" style="color: <%= opponent_label_color(opponent, team) %>"><%= opponent.short_name %></span>
          <% else %>
            <span class="text-[10px] lg:text-sm italic" style="color: <%= pal[:fg_soft] %>">bye</span>
          <% end %>
        </p>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
  </button>
</div>
